"<strong>Q1.</strong> V79 cells have an OER of {#} at {#} Gy and {#} at {#} Gy, but T1 cells have {#} at {#} Gy and {#} at {#} Gy. Use the low and high dose limits $$\\alpha_{air}/\\alpha_{hyp}$$ and $$\\sqrt{\\beta_{air}/\\beta_{hyp}}$$ to explain why the two go opposite ways.",
"<strong>Q2.</strong> At {#} Gy the V79 dose ratio is {#} without oxygen, {#} at {#} mmHg and {#} at {#} mmHg. Why does tumor hypoxia matter so much for radiotherapy while the difference between venous and arterial blood hardly does?",
"<strong>Q3.</strong> A group plates {#} cells at {#} Gy and counts {#}, {#} and {#} colonies. What went wrong, and how should they plate instead?",
"<strong>Q4.</strong> {#} Gy in one fraction gives late responding tissue (α/β {#} Gy) the effect of {#} Gy in {#} Gy fractions and a tumor (α/β {#} Gy) that of {#} Gy. Keeping the late effect of {#} Gy in {#} fixed, five fractions give only {#} Gy in all and a tumor EQD2 of {#} Gy. Why does fractionation spare late responding tissue, and when would fewer fractions be better?",
